00:03:47,090 --> 00:03:53,090
to jump down and begin executing the lines of code for Q. And then when

38
00:03:53,090 --> 00:04:00,590
Q hits its exit point, its return point, somehow is to get back to P, and not just to any old

39
00:04:00,590 --> 00:04:07,750
place in P, but specifically to whatever came comes in P right after the call to Q. So

40
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:13,590
somehow we have to record the information about where the return should be to be to be able

41
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:16,810
to return to the correct place. So that's first of all, two forms.

